module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.lowering_rebuilds_an_authored_atom_without_its_occurrence

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data lowering_rebuilds_an_authored_atom_without_its_occurrence: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "lowering_rebuilds_an_authored_atom_without_its_occurrence" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: v2 lowering keeps an authored atom's spelling but rebuilds the node that carries it with OccurrenceSynthetic, or folds it into a Named edge label, so the normalized tree still says WHAT was written but no longer WHERE. The parse minted an OccurrenceId for the atom and recorded its extent in the SpanIndex (`v2.compiler.parse` `parse_mint_from_source`); after lowering, no node carries that id. A consumer that must address one occurrence cannot find it: a located diagnostic at the reference, an occurrence-exact rewrite (XL-5), or a check that one mention survived rather than some other mention of the same name.",
    "SPECIMENS BY SYMBOL (re-measured on main 69e0bb7566e; docs/plans/lowering-occurrence-projection-design.md): type-position atoms are NO LONGER a specimen -- since #11985 `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_type_atom_node` builds them with `node_lowered_from` and they conserve. The reference-position specimens are two constructors. `v2.std.node_query` `construct_tag_edge` builds a record-literal tag or pattern constructor atom lowered from the ENCLOSING captured shell, so it carries the wrong source rather than none. `v2.std.qualified_name` `qualified_name_spine_node` builds every dotted-spine segment atom with `node_synthetic` inside its own item_node; its `occurrence_id` parameter reaches only the spine root. Its input is already `List<Symbol>`, because `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_postfix_chain_read` reduces the segment nodes to symbols upstream, so no caller could supply a per-segment source today. Declaration names, parameters, field names and argument labels become Named edge labels; those are binders and labels, not references.",
    "HOW IT SURFACED: `v2.compiler.reference_conservation` keys every authored parse atom by its minted occurrence and asks the normalized tree to account for it. Measured on main fec339d561 over `v2.compiler.reference_conservation_census` `reference_conservation_stratified_sample_paths`, only a minority of authored atoms keep their occurrence. The instrument that re-derives the split is `reference_conservation_stratified_sample_census`. The check reports these atoms as `locus_erased`, a separate count, and never as conserved.",
    "HARM: silent at the reference census, which keys by spelling and containment and so still counts these mentions. Not silent for anything occurrence-keyed. A diagnostic cannot point at the mention. A rewrite cannot target one occurrence of a repeated name. And a conservation check cannot tell a rebuilt atom from a dropped one without falling back to a spelling match inside the declaration, which is exactly the fallback `v2.compiler.reference_conservation` has to carry today (the declaration-scoped, multiset-consumed pool behind `locus_erased`).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The loss is now counted per module by the conservation check, not prevented. CEILING: structurally impossible on the lowering route, when every lowering constructor of a reference-position atom REQUIRES the authored terminal node it consumed and builds with `v2.std.node` `node_lowered_from(source: ...)`, carrying `std.occurrence_identity` OccurrenceMinted unchanged. NOT OccurrenceProjected: `std.occurrence_identity` reserves that arm for an insertion minted in a different allocator and says a carried-forward node gets no arm, so using it for same-graph lowering would be a second identity for one fact. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: every reference-position atom that lowering rebuilds carries its authored terminal's occurrence. When it holds, the reference-position share of `locus_erased` reads zero on each site's controlled fixture. Binders, field names, argument labels and module-header segments are OUT of this capability: stripping imports cannot make resolve refuse at them, so they are not in the XL-2 residual. Deleting the declaration-scoped spelling pool in `v2.compiler.reference_conservation` therefore also needs binders told apart from references by grammar role rather than by spelling. Recorded by the XL-2 manager as its own XL-2 prerequisite.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
